strata-by-luminaire for Debian
------------------------------

Only a packed binary was released (strata_by_jontte__cyndis__jnalanko.bin
on scene.org). The executable has been unpacked and renamed.

The binary was also patched to remove fullscreen (SDL 1.2 breaks the
display). This patch is already in the orig tarball.

At build time, debian/patch-binary.pl patches a copy of the executable
(build/strata-by-luminaire), the orig tarball is not modified:
 - the intro reused stack slots as arguments for glCompileShader(),
   glLinkProgram() and glUseProgram(). Current NVIDIA drivers overwrite
   them, glUseProgram() got a garbage id and the window stayed white. The
   calls jump to a trampoline, written in the zero padding at the end of
   the code segment, that pushes their arguments again;
 - at the end, the intro fell through into another function and crashed
   with a segmentation fault; it now calls exit_group(0);
 - the unused program header 1, which held garbage, becomes PT_GNU_STACK:
   the stack is no longer executable;
 - the fragment shader is replaced by debian/shader.frag, same length:
   "#version 130" (Mesa refused the shader without #version), explicit
   type conversions, and the time uniform declared before the texture,
   since the intro sets uniform location 0. With NVIDIA, the pictures are
   identical to the original shader.
The script checks the original bytes before patching.

The launcher sets SDL12COMPAT_SYNC_TO_VBLANK=1: the intro does not ask for
V-Sync itself. It plays the music with pw-play when PipeWire runs, else
paplay, else aplay: aplay goes through the ALSA default device, which only
reaches PipeWire when pipewire-alsa is installed for the architecture of
aplay (amd64 on a 64-bit system, so a dependency of this i386 package on
pipewire-alsa would not help).

The executable is a hand-made ELF without section headers: objdump and
dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read it, so the libraries are declared by hand in
debian/control, dh_strip, dh_dwz, dh_makeshlibs and dh_shlibdeps are
skipped in debian/rules. It links only libSDL, libGL and libpthread and
cannot be hardened: the lintian tags about libc and hardening are
overridden.

executable seems to be compiled for an unknown distribution

no GCC version string left in the executable

Source files:
-------------
none (no section headers, no symbol table)

